  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-p2700.html",
  "prefLabel": "He-P 2709.01 Variances",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-P 2709.01 Variances.\n\n(a) Applicants or license holders seeking variances from specific rules shall contact the department by telephone at (603) 271-4589 or by mail, to obtain a VR Form “Milk Variance Request Form” (February 2021).\n\n(b) Applicants or license holders shall complete and submit to the department VR Form “Milk Variance Request Form” (February 2021) by mailing to:\n\nDepartment of Health and Human Services\n\nDivision of Public Health Services\n\nFood Protection Section\n\n29 Hazen Dr.\n\nConcord, NH 03301\n\n(c) By completing and submitting a VR Form “Milk Variance Request Form” (February 2021), the applicant or licensee holder acknowledges that:\n\n(1) The requested variance pertains to the rule mentioned in the variance request only, and shall not be deemed permission to waiver from any other requirements outlined in the He-P 2700; and\n\n(2) If approved, this variance shall be considered null and void at such time one or more of the following events should occur:\n\na. Change of ownership;\n\nb. Renovation; or\n\nc. Failure to comply with said variance.\n\n(d) The commissioner shall approve a request for variance if:\n\n(1) The commissioner concludes that authorizing deviation from strict compliance with the rule item from which a variance is sought does not contradict the intent of the rule; and\n\n(2) The alternative proposed by the applicant or license holder ensures that the objective or intent of the rule item from which a variance is sought will be accomplished.\n\n(e) If a variance is approved, the license holder’s subsequent compliance with the alternatives approved in the variance shall be considered equivalent to complying with the rule item from which a variance was sought.\n\n(f) A variance shall be approved until the expiration of the current license or as specified by the department.\n\n(g) No request for a variance concerning the rules of other state agencies which are referred to in this chapter shall be approved.\n\nSource. #13175, eff 3-2-21\n\nAppendix",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-p2700.html"
}
